# ── Production (Vercel) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real values live in Vercel > Project (webwithirfan) > Settings >
# Environment Variables. They are injected at build time on every deploy.
# Never commit a file containing real values; .gitignore blocks *.env / .env.*.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY — Web3Forms access key (https://web3forms.com),
#                       created for info@webwithirfan.com. Set it for the
#                       Production environment (add Preview too if preview
#                       deploys should send real emails). The key is public by
#                       design and ships in the client bundle, but keep it out
#                       of git so rotating it stays a one-place change.
#                       Recipients: primary info@webwithirfan.com, with
#                       mirfanawan545@gmail.com as CC (configured in the
#                       Web3Forms dashboard for this key).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — public site origin, used for canonical/OG URLs and
#                       the generated sitemap.xml / robots.txt.
#
# NOTE: after the Next.js migration the old VITE_* names are dead. Add the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables in Vercel before merging, then delete the VITE_ ones.
#
# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the key:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# With no key set the contact form falls back to a prefilled mailto:, so local
# dev works without one — you just will not exercise the real Web3Forms path.

NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://webwithirfan.com
